speechtext:
It is my duty, pursuant to Standing Order 46, to inform the House that the questions to be raised tonight at the time of adjournment are as follows: The Hon. Member for Don Valley East (Mr. Attewell)- Social Affairs-Abuse of the elderly; the Hon. Member for Winnipeg-Birds Hill (Mr. Blaikie)-Environmental Affairs
(a)	Canada-United States discussions (b) Canadian position;
the Hon. Member for Algoma (Mr. Foster)-Farm Credit Corporation-Moratorium on foreclosures.
